# Build context hygiene. The repo working tree is 3.9 GB, almost all of it artifacts the
# image either mounts at runtime or rebuilds; sending that to the daemon would dominate
# every build's wall time and cache-bust on any index rebuild.
.git
.venv
.pytest_cache
.cache
.deepeval
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Secrets never enter the build context. COPY . . with a .env present bakes the key into
# a layer, and layers survive `docker run --rm` and travel with `docker push`.
.env
.env.bak.*
requirements.txt.stale

# 961 MB of FAISS indexes and 192 MB of chunk parquet. Mounted as a volume by compose
# (see docker-compose.yml) rather than baked, because they are rebuildable, they change
# far more often than the code, and a cold `docker build` should not move a gigabyte.
data/
mlflow.db
mlruns/
notes/

# Model weights are baked (see Dockerfile), but from the Hub in a dedicated layer, not
# copied out of the developer's local cache — that cache is 757 MB and holds every model
# the ablation ever touched, not the two the image actually serves.

# 148 MB of per-run evaluation detail, each record carrying the full retrieved passage
# text. /eval-report reads evals/history.jsonl (72 KB) and never opens these, so the image
# gains nothing from them. Compose mounts ./evals read-only for the runs that do want them.
evals/results/
evals/*.bak.*
